{"title":"DOGE is having some issues","link":"https://www.garbageday.email/p/doge-is-having-some-issues","date":1740143839000,"content":"<div><div><p><i>Welcome to Garbage Weekend. It’s the internet garbage you know and love, but in a format that’s easier to read while you wait for the various horrors to cease.</i></p><div><img src=\"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=80/uploads/asset/file/84af6838-f80d-4f98-b65e-bdd6dfc6e9ee/GettyImages-2200059458.jpg?t=1740137438\" /><div><span><p>(Photo by SAUL LOEB/AFP via Getty Images)</p></span></div></div><p>This week, the Department of Government Efficiency (DOGE) ran into some barriers, like having to <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/story/doge-elon-musk-leadership-administrator/?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues\" target=\"_blank\">pretend Elon Musk isn’t in charge</a> or <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/story/elon-musk-doge-social-security-150-year-old-benefits/?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues\" target=\"_blank\">not understanding the code</a> government databases use. This is a <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/jakemgrumbach.bsky.social/post/3lhi76uc4yk2b?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues\" target=\"_blank\">crack team</a>, who’s brought us such wonders as a <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/18/the-people-in-elon-musk-doge-universe/?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues#ethan-shaotran\" target=\"_blank\">Trump-themed </a><i><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/18/the-people-in-elon-musk-doge-universe/?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues#ethan-shaotran\" target=\"_blank\">Crossy Road </a></i><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/18/the-people-in-elon-musk-doge-universe/?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues#ethan-shaotran\" target=\"_blank\">clone</a>. After all, gaming is the future, that’s why <i>Pokémon Go </i>may be <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2025/02/18/pokemon-go-maker-niantic-is-reportedly-selling-its-games-division/?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues\" target=\"_blank\">selling to the Saudis</a>, and why <i>Marvel Rivals </i>earning <a href=\"https://fictionhorizon.com/marvel-rivals-reaches-financial-milestone/?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues\" target=\"_blank\">$100 million in a month</a> isn’t enough to <a href=\"https://www.engadget.com/gaming/marvel-rivals-team-hit-with-layoffs-despite-huge-success-of-game-133002120.html?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues\" target=\"_blank\">pay the game director</a>. At least the <i>real</i> most popular online game is thriving, as hundreds of people place <a href=\"https://manifold.markets/cash/will-pope-francis-cease-to-be-pope-623916036ab8?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues\" target=\"_blank\">bets on the next Pope</a>! </p><p>Oh well, here’s some fun stuff…</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/rosalarian.bsky.social/post/3lifkfkxz6s2q?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues\" target=\"_blank\">A great custom car</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mdfoodieboyz/video/7471066852647521566?utm_source=www.garbageday.email&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=doge-is-having-some-issues\" target=\"_blank\">Middle schooler podcast</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DGElameyxyX/?utm_source=www